l/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1474]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Autosomal dominant</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1475]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Single gene defect HOX gene</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1476]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><em><strong>Classification:</strong></em></span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1477]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Type </strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>I</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>: (64%)</strong></span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1478]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Typical, symmetrical </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>uterovaginal </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>aplasia/Hypoplasia</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1479]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Tubes + ovaries Normal, uterine buds Present</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1480]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Type II: (24%)</strong></span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1481]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Atypical, Asymmetrical UV aplasia</span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>/h</span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>ypoplasia</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1482]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Tubal Hypo</span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>plasia</span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>/Aplasia one or both</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1483]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Ovarian malformation one or both</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1484]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><u>+</u></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> Renal Anomalies</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1485]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Type III: 12% MURCS Syndrome: </strong></span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[1486]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: ##2F5496; font-family: \"Aptos\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Mullerian aplasia </span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" dat